                <div class="info-box tip"><h5>🎯 Chapter 4 Exam Prep — VLANs &amp; 802.1Q</h5><p><strong>Exam Weight: MEDIUM (8-10% of questions)</strong></p><div class="card-grid"><div class="info-card"><h5>📋 Must Memorize</h5><ul><li>802.1Q tag: 4 bytes (TPID=0x8100 + PCP/DEI/VID 12-bit=4094 VLANs)</li><li>Access port: single untagged VLAN; Trunk port: multiple tagged VLANs</li><li>Native VLAN: untagged frames on trunk (default VLAN 1)</li><li>VLAN hopping: double-tagging attack mitigation</li></ul></div><div class="info-card"><h5>⚠️ Common Traps</h5><ul><li>VLAN 1 is the default native VLAN — change it for security!</li><li>Untagged frames on trunk use the native VLAN</li><li>802.1Q tag adds 4 bytes → frame size up to 1522 bytes</li><li>Inter-VLAN routing requires L3 device (router or L3 switch)</li></ul></div><div class="info-card"><h5>🔧 Quick Commands</h5><ul><li><code>ip link add link eth0 name eth0.10 type vlan id 10</code></li><li><code>cat /proc/net/vlan/config</code> — VLAN config</li><li><code>bridge vlan show</code> — Bridge VLAN table</li></ul></div></div></div>
