    '6' = @'
                <div class="info-box tip"><h5>🎯 Chapter 6 Exam Prep — Routing Fundamentals</h5><p><strong>Exam Weight: HIGH (12-15% of questions)</strong></p><div class="card-grid"><div class="info-card"><h5>📋 Must Memorize</h5><ul><li>Longest prefix match: more specific route wins over less specific</li><li>Default route: 0.0.0.0/0 (matches everything, lowest priority)</li><li>Administrative distance: Connected=0, Static=1, OSPF=110, BGP(eBGP=20,iBGP=200)</li><li>Routing table selection: Longest match → AD → Metric</li></ul></div><div class="info-card"><h5>⚠️ Common Traps</h5><ul><li>ip route get DST shows which route will be used (test before deploy!)</li><li>Asymmetric routing: forward path != return path → firewall drops</li><li>Missing return route is the #1 cause of "can ping but can't connect"</li><li>Routing loops: TTL prevents infinite loops (max 255, default 64)</li></ul></div><div class="info-card"><h5>🔧 Quick Commands</h5><ul><li><code>ip route show</code> — View routing table</li><li><code>ip route get 8.8.8.8</code> — Route lookup test</li><li><code>ip route add 10.0.0.0/8 via 192.168.1.254</code></li><li><code>traceroute -n HOST</code> — Per-hop path</li></ul></div></div></div>
