                <div class="info-box tip"><h5>🎯 Chapter 7 Exam Prep — Dynamic Routing (OSPF/BGP)</h5><p><strong>Exam Weight: MEDIUM (8-10% of questions)</strong></p><div class="card-grid"><div class="info-card"><h5>📋 Must Memorize</h5><ul><li>OSPF: Link-state, Area 0(backbone), DR/BDR on broadcast networks, multicast 224.0.0.5/6</li><li>BGP: Path-vector, TCP/179, AS-path for loop prevention</li><li>eBGP(AS-to-AS, AD=20) vs iBGP(within AS, AD=200)</li><li>OSPF states: Down→Init→2-Way→ExStart→Exchange→Loading→Full</li></ul></div><div class="info-card"><h5>⚠️ Common Traps</h5><ul><li>iBGP full mesh requirement (or route reflectors/confederations)</li><li>OSPF areas must connect to Area 0 (backbone)</li><li>BGP does NOT automatically load balance (multipath must be configured)</li><li>IGP(OSPF/EIGRP) + BGP: IGP for reachability, BGP for policy</li></ul></div><div class="info-card"><h5>🔧 Quick Commands</h5><ul><li><code>ip route show protocol bgp</code> — BGP routes</li><li><code>birdc show protocols</code> — BIRD routing daemon</li><li><code>vtysh -c "show ip ospf neighbor"</code> — OSPF neighbors</li></ul></div></div></div>
