    '8' = @'
                <div class="info-box tip"><h5>🎯 Chapter 8 Exam Prep — TCP Deep Dive</h5><p><strong>Exam Weight: VERY HIGH (15-20% of questions)</strong></p><div class="card-grid"><div class="info-card"><h5>📋 Must Memorize</h5><ul><li>3-way handshake: SYN→, ←SYN-ACK, ACK→ (ESTABLISHED)</li><li>4-way close: FIN→, ←ACK, ←FIN, ACK→ (TIME_WAIT=2MSL)</li><li>TCP states: LISTEN, SYN_SENT/RECVD, ESTABLISHED, FIN_WAIT1/2, TIME_WAIT, CLOSE_WAIT</li><li>Flow control: sliding window (rwnd); Congestion control: cwnd (CUBIC/BBR)</li></ul></div><div class="info-card"><h5>⚠️ Common Traps</h5><ul><li>TIME_WAIT: 2MSL(60s) — normal, not a problem (tcp_tw_reuse)</li><li>CLOSE_WAIT: app didn't call close() → socket leak (check ss -tpn)</li><li>Connection refused(RST) vs Timeout(SYN dropped by firewall)</li><li>TCP retransmits = packet loss signal, not necessarily congestion</li></ul></div><div class="info-card"><h5>🔧 Quick Commands</h5><ul><li><code>ss -tpn state established</code> — Active connections</li><li><code>ss -tin | grep retrans</code> — Retransmit counters</li><li><code>tcpdump -i any 'tcp[tcpflags] & (tcp-syn|tcp-fin) != 0'</code> — Flag filter</li></ul></div></div></div>
