    '9' = @'
                <div class="info-box tip"><h5>🎯 Chapter 9 Exam Prep — UDP &amp; Transport Layer</h5><p><strong>Exam Weight: MEDIUM (8% of questions)</strong></p><div class="card-grid"><div class="info-card"><h5>📋 Must Memorize</h5><ul><li>UDP: Connectionless, 8B header, no retransmission, no ordering</li><li>Common UDP: DNS:53, DHCP:67/68, NTP:123, SNMP:161, QUIC:443, VoIP/RTP</li><li>TCP vs UDP: reliable/ordered vs fast/low-overhead</li><li>QUIC: UDP-based, built-in TLS 1.3, 0-RTT handshake, HTTP/3 uses it</li></ul></div><div class="info-card"><h5>⚠️ Common Traps</h5><ul><li>"UDP is unreliable" — but QUIC adds reliability at the application layer</li><li>UDP checksum is optional in IPv4 (MANDATORY in IPv6)</li><li>traceroute traditionally uses UDP (high ports) — newer versions use TCP</li><li>DNS uses BOTH UDP(queries) and TCP(zone transfers, large responses)</li></ul></div><div class="info-card"><h5>🔧 Quick Commands</h5><ul><li><code>ss -ulpn</code> — UDP listeners</li><li><code>nc -uz HOST PORT</code> — UDP connectivity test</li><li><code>tcpdump -i any udp port 53</code> — Capture UDP DNS</li></ul></div></div></div>
