    '10' = @'
                <div class="info-box tip"><h5>🎯 Chapter 10 Exam Prep — ICMP &amp; Diagnostics</h5><p><strong>Exam Weight: HIGH (10-12% of questions)</strong></p><div class="card-grid"><div class="info-card"><h5>📋 Must Memorize</h5><ul><li>ICMP types: 0(Echo Reply), 8(Echo Request), 3(Dest Unreachable), 11(TTL Exceeded)</li><li>Dest Unreachable codes: 0(Net), 1(Host), 3(Port), 4(Frag needed/DF set)</li><li>traceroute: TTL=1,2,3... + ICMP Type 11 from each hop</li><li>PMTU discovery: uses ICMP "frag needed" (type 3 code 4)</li></ul></div><div class="info-card"><h5>⚠️ Common Traps</h5><ul><li>ping tests L1-L3 ONLY — does NOT test TCP ports (use nc -zv)!</li><li>Firewalls often allow ICMP but block TCP → "ping works, app doesn't"</li><li>PMTU black hole: ICMP frag-needed blocked → TCP stalls (MSS clamping fix)</li><li>ICMP rate limiting: some hosts limit ICMP replies → packet loss false positive</li></ul></div><div class="info-card"><h5>🔧 Quick Commands</h5><ul><li><code>ping -c 10 -i 0.2 HOST</code> — Fast ping</li><li><code>mtr -r HOST</code> — Combined ping+traceroute</li><li><code>traceroute -n -T HOST</code> — TCP traceroute</li></ul></div></div></div>
