                <div class="info-box tip"><h5>🎯 Chapter 16 Exam Prep — Firewalls &amp; iptables/nftables</h5><p><strong>Exam Weight: HIGH (10-12% of questions)</strong></p><div class="card-grid"><div class="info-card"><h5>📋 Must Memorize</h5><ul><li>iptables chains: INPUT, OUTPUT, FORWARD, PREROUTING(DNAT), POSTROUTING(SNAT)</li><li>Tables: filter(default), nat, mangle, raw, security</li><li>Targets: ACCEPT, DROP(silent), REJECT(ICMP), LOG, RETURN, DNAT, SNAT, MASQUERADE</li><li>nftables: modern replacement, unified syntax, better performance</li></ul></div><div class="info-card"><h5>⚠️ Common Traps</h5><ul><li>DROP vs REJECT: DROP causes timeout, REJECT gives instant feedback</li><li>Rule order matters! First match wins (put ESTABLISHED,RELATED early)</li><li>iptables rules are NOT persistent by default (iptables-save needed)</li><li>FORWARD chain is for routed traffic (not local processes)</li></ul></div><div class="info-card"><h5>🔧 Quick Commands</h5><ul><li><code>iptables -L -nv --line-numbers</code> — List rules</li><li><code>iptables-save > /etc/iptables/rules.v4</code> — Persist</li><li><code>nft list ruleset</code> — nftables view</li></ul></div></div></div>
