                <div class="info-box tip"><h5>🎯 Chapter 18 Exam Prep — Kubernetes Pod Networking</h5><p><strong>Exam Weight: VERY HIGH (15-20% of questions)</strong></p><div class="card-grid"><div class="info-card"><h5>📋 Must Memorize</h5><ul><li>Pod: shared network namespace (same IP, localhost, ports across containers)</li><li>CNI: ADD/DEL/CHECK/VERSION operations; config in /etc/cni/net.d/</li><li>veth pairs: one end in pod NS, other attached to cni0 bridge on node</li><li>IP-per-pod model: every pod gets a unique, routable IP</li></ul></div><div class="info-card"><h5>⚠️ Common Traps</h5><ul><li>Pod IPs are ephemeral — always use Services for stable addressing</li><li>Container port conflicts within a pod (shared NS means shared ports!)</li><li>hostNetwork: true bypasses CNI entirely (security risk!)</li><li>CNI plugin must handle IPAM, routing, and potentially NetworkPolicy</li></ul></div><div class="info-card"><h5>🔧 Quick Commands</h5><ul><li><code>kubectl exec POD -- ip addr</code> — Pod interfaces</li><li><code>kubectl exec POD -- ip route</code> — Pod routing</li><li><code>kubectl get pods -o wide</code> — Pod IPs &amp; nodes</li></ul></div></div></div>
